hen calming down works for *their* body, and they use it masterfully. That’s a testament to their self-awareness. But it doesn’t mean the same would work for someone else whose airway is already severely clamped, or that they themselves might never need their inhaler in a more serious episode. So I wouldn’t say “it doesn’t work like that.” I’d say: “It works exactly like that for certain types and stages of breathing difficulty, which is why it’s such a great tool in your friend’s toolkit. And for severe attacks, the toolkit requires the medication to open the airway first—then calm can do its job.”
